    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d899">

                <pb facs="0809" n="797" xml:id="pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/582: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-20T16:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>289. Your 636, June 19, 1 p.m. General Arnold is in accord with the Department’s
                    views that the Department’s telegram no. 287, June 19, 5 p.m. affords adequate
                    basis for action you suggest in your telegram under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
